Z||000004||Slammed Fiero||06-18-2001||02:38 PM||||Cross fire motors were nasty things! We had one on the garage floor for 2 years out of an 84 vette. They used 2 throttle bodies facing upwards. Looked like a relative to the cross ram manifolds of 60's chryslers.<P>Vipers use Twin throttle bodies , GM's late 90's incarnation of the Zl1 Camaro used twin TPI throttle bodies...<P>In the fiero's case the intake manifold is a restriction. I remember seeing the PPG pace car a few years back , they modified the intake extensively... I'm not sure , but I believe this is why the fiero falls on it's face in higher rpm/s.<P>Our 3.8 911 uses a single TB for each cylinder...looks like modern tripple webbers.<BR>They seemed to move the power band up a bit over the stock setup , but the power seems endless..no flat spots in the Torque curve..We also found this with our corvair , the 2.9ltr flat 6 loves to rev and creat power with it's tripple webbers..not as much down low as compared to the holley 390 , but the top end is nothing short of astounding ..espically at redline of 8000rpm<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||06-18-2001||02:52 PM||||The "Cease-Fire" engines are twin TBI. They actually run pretty good when they are working right.||||reg||1
Z||000006||mrfixit58||06-18-2001||05:14 PM||||Mine ran great. It road like crap but that's a different story.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||6
Z||000007||84Bill||06-18-2001||05:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by terryk:<BR><B>The "Cease-Fire" engines are twin TBI. They actually run pretty good when they are working right.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I almost would not mind having a crossfire equiped car right now but I guess thats because I'm older now and my feebel mind can't remember the awfull nightmare they were to get setup right.<P>||||reg||1
