Z||000010||Slammed Fiero||06-19-2001||12:03 AM||||Switched to TPI in 85<BR>Switched to Aluminum Heads in mid 86<BR>although all 86 Converts were fitted with aluminum heads..only later coupes were aluminum head equiped.<P>the 84 pulled 7 sec to sixty , voted car and driver car of the year (Fiero was in the running) the 84 z51 was the best (skidpad wise) handling car in the US until the 2000 ZO6 vette. over 1 G on the skid pad , rode like a shoppin cart.<P>Crossfire was first put into use in the 82 vette<BR>there was no 83 vette<BR>Cross fires have the same problem fiero's do , they don't breath.<P><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Pontiaddict||06-19-2001||02:15 PM||||Most of gm's efi intakes use really long narrow runners. For GM it was a good thing, without having to feed a motor at 7000 rpms then they could get higher average fuel economy ratings, the same thing with a smaller motor that has alot (relatively) of low end torque. (A 2.8 or a 305tpi in a firebird for example) Of course it reallt didn't make for a performance motor It was just current thinking at the time. <P>I like BMW's intake design. A common plenum with runners feeding into a throttle body for each cylinder. It's a rather low compromise design that seems to work well.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Slammed Fiero||06-19-2001||02:40 PM||||When our 87 Vette was stock with the exception of 3.23 gears it would get 26mpg on the highway in overdrive.<P>Doug Nash 4+3 7spd..<P>although it fell flat on it's face above 4800 rpm. But the Torque was amazing (L98) In pro Solo's it would sit right beside Zr1's half way down the course!<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
